## Minimal local successor

The v3 acquisition adapter authenticates the exact frozen v2 bytes before
compilation. Only schema, workflow name, CI flag, approved parent and output
bindings change. Download limits, software hashes, ownership checks, consumed
attempt state and retirement behavior remain frozen. The v2 temporary-input
prefix stays unchanged because its exact retirement regex requires it; each
future fresh VM still creates a unique owned directory.

The v3 verifier authenticates source bytes before execution, performs bounded
stable nofollow reads, rejects noncanonical/duplicate-key/float JSON, reuses the
unchanged native receipt validator, and additionally binds the prefix receipt.
Preflight modes do not write receipts. The receipt writer creates a private,
exclusive file and does not overwrite previous verification.

The proposed workflow keeps cleanup and qualification on the **same fresh VM**:
complete first-ten-child audit/removal, frozen setup probe, closed receipt check
and current free-space measurement, then bounded acquisition, unchanged native
supervisor, exact input retirement and receipt verification. Insufficient space
stops before download. No broader deletion or extra attempt is selected.

The test runner uses the established no-site unittest command with `tests/path`
for namespace-package imports. Runtime entrypoints still use `-I -S -B`.

