## Next authority boundary

Fresh approval is needed for the plan's exact five-file publication and combined
one-shot remote job, including another freshly audited prefix cleanup on its own
disposable VM. The proposed acquisition makes four HTTPS requests to the bound
private GitHub artifact and signed blob endpoint, downloads the exact
1,062,113,436-byte CPU software ZIP, and retains/extracts only the bound software.
It is not public-only or zero-network. No artifact substitute, rebuild or retry
is allowed. Availability must be checked before publication; it was not refreshed
in this local-only step.

The intended activated workflow is byte-bound in the plan. Only its exact
one-line guard replacement is proposed; it has **not** been applied. Ordinary
Source/Spark CI would also run after a later approved push. No other local file,
private data or historical receipt belongs in that publication.

Gate 5 remains incomplete until actual native qualification and remaining
host/import prerequisites are satisfied. The old native failure is preserved;
